  "finding": "P(matched | fired) is >= 0.98 above 27 GeV and 1.000 above 35 GeV, so the MATCHING requirement costs essentially nothing there. The slow rise of the combined efficiency is P(Ele27 fired): the trigger's own efficiency relative to our offline Medium electron definition (HLT WPTight is tighter than offline Medium, and the L1 EG seed has its own turn-on). No matched-electron pT threshold can remove that -- it is a property of the trigger, not of the threshold.",
